1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,823
Hi, I’m Obinna.

2
00:00:01,963 --> 00:00:06,144
Welcome to Learn Anywhere, an app for learning with limited connectivity.

3
00:00:06,284 --> 00:00:10,432
We begin with fresh local learning state on the iPhone simulator.

4
00:00:10,572 --> 00:00:18,517
We will choose preferences, find a course, read its lessons, try explanations, and explore the tools that help learners continue.

5
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,735
The first step is language selection.

6
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:28,431
Learn Anywhere supports English, French, Portuguese, Arabic, Hausa, Yoruba, and Igbo.

7
00:00:28,571 --> 00:00:32,176
I select English for this demonstration and apply the choice.

8
00:00:32,316 --> 00:00:37,329
Available learning content can download during setup, so setup uses a connection.

9
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,703
Next comes the optional learner profile.

10
00:00:42,843 --> 00:00:48,559
You can personalize the experience and choose whether lessons should start with the shorter explained version.

11
00:00:48,699 --> 00:00:53,807
No email, password, or real personal information is required for this walkthrough.

12
00:00:53,947 --> 00:00:57,796
I leave the optional details empty and skip ahead to the main app.

13
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:02,533
Home is the starting point for learning.

14
00:01:02,673 --> 00:01:05,391
It combines course access and reading progress.

15
00:01:05,531 --> 00:01:10,746
Setup may already have saved an available pack, but choosing a course is a separate action.

16
00:01:10,886 --> 00:01:15,610
Opening a lesson alone does not mean that its reading or assessment is complete.

17
00:01:20,391 --> 00:01:23,216
Discover is where learners find published courses.

18
00:01:23,353 --> 00:01:27,763
Each card introduces the subject and offers a way to open its contents.

19
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:32,331
This demonstration uses the original AI for Everyday Tasks course.

20
00:01:32,468 --> 00:01:39,163
New discovery and missing downloads need a connection; the saved library gives us a separate place to return later.

21
00:01:40,400 --> 00:01:43,844
The course contents provide an ordered path through the material.

22
00:01:43,984 --> 00:01:49,092
Here we can see six lessons, their reading state, and the language saved on this device.

23
00:01:49,232 --> 00:01:52,602
Opening a course fetches a missing language pack when needed.

24
00:01:52,742 --> 00:01:54,929
Choose a lesson and begin at the top.

25
00:02:00,371 --> 00:02:04,360
The regular lesson combines readable text with practical activities.

26
00:02:04,490 --> 00:02:08,953
Its reading estimate and Ready offline status help explain what is available.

27
00:02:09,083 --> 00:02:15,122
Read aloud offers another way to engage using an available device voice, with a speed control nearby.

28
00:02:15,252 --> 00:02:19,170
Playback starts in this demo; I pause and stop it before continuing.

29
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,238
The teal lightbulb switches the same page to its explained version.

30
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:29,081
This substitutes a shorter, simpler explanation for the regular lesson body.

31
00:02:29,221 --> 00:02:33,039
It does not open a different course or change the final assessment.

32
00:02:33,179 --> 00:02:38,147
A learner can use this view to grasp the main idea, then return to the fuller teaching.

33
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:43,119
Both versions support learning at your own pace.

34
00:02:43,259 --> 00:02:48,708
The explanation is saved content rather than a fresh response generated for every tap.

35
00:02:48,848 --> 00:02:52,943
Switching views starts reading at the top again, while progress stays separate.

36
00:02:53,083 --> 00:02:57,722
The bookmark icon also offers a quick way to keep a lesson for a later visit.

37
00:03:00,367 --> 00:03:03,207
Back at the course contents, I open the final quiz.

38
00:03:03,335 --> 00:03:05,587
A question presents four answer choices.

39
00:03:05,716 --> 00:03:11,237
Selecting one enables the next question, and answers are saved locally as the learner proceeds.

40
00:03:11,366 --> 00:03:19,171
This walkthrough stops before submission: we are demonstrating the assessment flow, without claiming a completed course, final score, or result.

41
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:24,505
Language can also be changed after setup using the globe control.

42
00:03:24,645 --> 00:03:26,737
Here I select French and apply it.

43
00:03:26,877 --> 00:03:30,171
A missing published translation downloads before it is used.

44
00:03:30,311 --> 00:03:38,311
The course can retain both English and French on this device, so choosing another language does not mean discarding the first saved pack.

45
00:03:40,400 --> 00:03:43,291
Downloads organizes the local course library.

46
00:03:43,431 --> 00:03:48,453
Its readiness labels and saved-language details make it easier to know what is stored.

47
00:03:48,593 --> 00:03:52,315
Learners can open a course or manage its languages from here.

48
00:03:52,455 --> 00:03:58,831
We show saved text readiness in this recording; we have not switched off the network to perform an offline test.

49
00:04:00,361 --> 00:04:03,675
Profile and settings let learners revisit their preferences.

50
00:04:03,802 --> 00:04:08,735
They can adjust the reading experience and choose whether explained lessons should be their starting view.

51
00:04:08,861 --> 00:04:13,168
These choices support different learning needs without requiring a learner account.

52
00:04:13,295 --> 00:04:19,173
The app remains a working proof of concept, with further translation review and deployment hardening still needed.

53
00:04:20,317 --> 00:04:25,638
Behind the interface, Flutter runs the app and SQLite stores downloaded packs and pending activity on the phone.

54
00:04:25,749 --> 00:04:29,051
A Quarkus backend serves published content from PostgreSQL.

55
00:04:29,162 --> 00:04:33,850
When synchronization succeeds, acknowledged event identifiers help avoid duplicate rewards.

56
00:04:33,961 --> 00:04:39,189
This architecture connects a local learning experience with centrally managed content and confirmed progress.

57
00:04:40,371 --> 00:04:47,288
Codex helped develop the app and backend, inspect learning flows, and produce documentation and demonstration materials.

58
00:04:47,418 --> 00:04:52,122
The next steps are learner testing, bilingual review, and a stronger production deployment.

59
00:04:52,252 --> 00:04:59,170
Learn Anywhere aims to make useful learning easier to return to: choose a course, save it, and continue at your own pace.
